From: retroforge
Subject: [PATCH] steamcompmgr: hold the boot splash until the shell draws

gamescope takes DRM master at its start, ~9 s into a boot on the MANGMI
Air X, and commits nothing until the shell's first frame, ~17 s. The
panel keeps the boot splash drawer's last frame through that gap, but
only a video-mode panel keeps showing the drawer's activity bar moving:
a command-mode one shows committed frames only, and the drawer can no
longer commit once it has dropped master.

The drawer now hands its frame over, in the file GAMESCOPE_BOOT_SPLASH
names: the frame as the panel scans it out, and the bar's frames as
strips of it. Until the shell is drawing, gamescope paints only that:
one screen-sized XRGB8888 layer, double buffered, with the next strip
copied into the buffer that is not on screen once per tick. The frames
are ordinary scanout images, with the modifiers the plane offers (UBWC
on msm). The layer is pre-rotated, so it scans out with no copy wherever
the panel takes a pre-rotated buffer (g_uPreRotation), and it is placed
the same on any rotation. A panel rotated in the composite, or a frame
drawn for another orientation, gets no splash.

The shell's first frame is not the end: OpenGamepadUI puts up one
empty, transparent frame and then loads for ~7 s before its next, which
was ~7 s of black between the splash and its boot video. The splash
goes once the shell has put up three frames within 0.5 s, 20 s after
its first frame at the latest, and 60 s after gamescope's start in any
case.

vulkan_upload_texture_rect() copies a rectangle into a texture, in bands
the upload buffer holds (one 1080p frame).

